    <Major></Major>
    <Description>Keyran v1.3.6 Macro is a specialized script for Grand Theft Auto V Roleplay (GTA 5 RP) on the FiveM platform, designed to automate the Smelting process. This macro streamlines the smelting activity by simulating keypresses for "E" and selecting the top available option in the smelting menu every 25-30 seconds. The script is optimized for a screen resolution of 1920x1080.

Features:

Smelting Automation:

The macro automates the Smelting process in GTA 5 RP, allowing for hands-free operation.
Simulates the "E" keypress to initiate smelting and selects the top available option in the smelting menu.
Interval-based Execution:

The script operates on a timed basis, triggering smelting actions every 25-30 seconds.
Optimal timing for resource efficiency and in-game realism.
Resolution Compatibility:

Specifically configured for a screen resolution of 1920x1080, ensuring accurate positioning of the cursor for menu selection.
User-Friendly Interface:

Simple and straightforward setup, making it accessible for users with varying levels of technical expertise.
Customizable settings available within the script for easy adaptation to different scenarios.
Anti-Detection Measures:

Incorporates anti-detection features to reduce the likelihood of server or anti-cheat systems identifying the automation.
Randomized intervals and cursor movements contribute to a more natural interaction with the game.
Usage Instructions:

Installation:

Copy and paste the script into the designated directory within the FiveM client.
Resolution Adjustment:

Ensure that your game is set to a screen resolution of 1920x1080 for optimal performance.
Configuration:

Open the script using a text editor to adjust settings if necessary (interval duration, etc.).
Save the changes.
Execution:

Run the macro within the GTA 5 RP session using the designated key or command.
Caution:

Use the macro responsibly and in accordance with server rules to avoid potential repercussions.
Disclaimer:
This macro is intended for entertainment purposes only. The developers and distributors of this script are not responsible for any consequences resulting from the use of this macro, including server bans or other penalties.</Description>
